+++ b/docs/memory/decision-log/dl-002-inject-task-timestamps-at-the-list-boundary.md
@@ -0,0 +1,22 @@
+---
+id: dl-002-inject-task-timestamps-at-the-list-boundary
+type: decision-log
+title: "Inject task timestamps at the list boundary"
+status: pending
+format: 1
+---
+
+## Context
+
+Tasks need creation and last-change timestamps, while code under `src/domain/` must not read the
+wall clock.
+
+## Decision
+
+Inject a `now` function through the task-list factory. The public factory supplies a default
+ISO-8601 clock; the list stamps successful task creation and mutation results with its value.
+
+## Consequences
+
+The domain remains deterministic and callers may provide a fixed clock for tests. The public list
+factory gains an optional clock parameter.
